My understanding is that, if a monster is hostile to the player, the
pet will try to attack (unless it'd get stoned/paralyzed/killed by the
splash damage, or the monster is simply too high-level).  If, however,
the monster is peaceful to the player, the pet goes through a few more
checks before attacking--specifically, they won't attack peacefuls when
they're below 25% health, and they won't attack your quest leader or
his guardians (MS_GUARDIAN is the other yokels wandering around your
quest home, not a guardian angel; see monflag.h, line 44).

Thus, pets will try to protect you from hostile enemies even when they
are themselves badly hurt; they will not try to wipe out non-hostiles.
Watch Captains, etc., are (typically) peaceful, so the only time
they'll kill your pet is when they can take off more than 25% of your
pet's HP in a single round.  Of course, with the silver saber &
multiple attacks per round, this becomes a very real possibility...

